# Whats new in african dance

It has been such a pleasure to have Pascale teaching with us this year. Pascale has been teaching and performing West African dance and Flamenco for many years and amidst her busy life as a Naturopath, she is also one of the core members of the [Muso Foli Dance Troupe](https://www.facebook.com/Muso-Foli-Dance-Troupe-747132222053774/?fref=ts). Pascale has been filling in for Bec this year and dance students will definitely see more of her in 2016. Pascale will be teaching the rhythm Kpanlogo. Dancers, if you would like to keep updated on classes, events and news please join our Rhythm Culture Drum and Dance [Facebook page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/1735722343328787/). Also, to receive newsletters on exciting new workshops, please make sure you have given us your contact email address.  If you are interested in seeing Pascale and the Muso Foli Dance Troupe in action get down to the Rhythm Culture space at the Ocean St World 2016 Festival on Sunday March 27 at 4pm. African [dance classes](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7TABwEGiV1k) on Tuesday nights 6.30pm @ Palmwoods Memorial Hall $15
